# Use WireGuard And SSH

This guide covers secure device registration, tunnel setup, and SSH access.

## 1. Register a device

```bash
loom wg devices register --name "my-workstation"
loom wg devices list
```

## 2. Start a tunnel to one weaver

```bash
loom tunnel up --weaver <weaver-id>
loom tunnel status
```

When done:

```bash
loom tunnel down
```

## 3. SSH directly through Loom

```bash
loom ssh <weaver-id>
```

Useful flags:

```bash
loom ssh <weaver-id> --user loom --port 22 -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -- -L 3000:localhost:3000
```

## 4. Revoke old devices

```bash
loom wg devices revoke <device-id>
```

<Callout variant="warning" title="Current limitation">
	`tunnel up` currently requires `--weaver`; multi-weaver tunnel mode is not yet implemented.
</Callout>

## Server-side APIs involved

- `POST /api/wg/devices`
- `GET /api/wg/devices`
- `DELETE /api/wg/devices/{id}`
- `POST /api/wg/sessions`
- `GET /api/wg/sessions`
- `DELETE /api/wg/sessions/{id}`
- `GET /api/wg/derp-map`
